From 6fb5fcef313f5c3698eab4e30cbff015a4b668b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): a model switch refuses to publish onto a turn
 admitted after its snapshot [daveey]

The /model mirror and config.set model read session['running'] unlocked, then
switch_runtime resolves for seconds and publishes onto the live agent. A turn
admitted in that window ran its remaining API calls on the swapped model/client
(pre-fix the Event-ordered custody test saw agent.model == target after the
turn was admitted).

Fix reuses turn admission: admit_durable_turn_lease publishes its holder under
turn_admission_lock; the switch checks-and-publishes under the same lock and
raises TurnAdmittedDuringSwitch if a holder appeared since its snapshot. The
direct swap holds the lock too. _apply_model_switch catches the refusal and
stashes the pick via _stash_pending_model_switch (deferred=True) so it applies
at the next turn start.

Tests: test_managed_switch_turn_custody.py (parked switch, real turn; red
before/green after), test_model_switch_lost_turn_race.py. 251 related test
files pass; scripts/check health ok.
